## Completeness matrix for ninja.imports.scm — `include` and `subninja` are
## structurally identical in node-types.json (an unfielded `path` child,
## `multiple: false`, `required: true`), so there is exactly one shape per
## directive to exercise, plus a NEGATIVE section of near-miss constructs
## that must not be captured as imports.

# Variant 1: `include` — pulls target/rule/variable definitions into the
# current scope.
include rules.ninja

# Variant 2: `subninja` — pulls in a separate scoped sub-build.
subninja subdir/build.ninja

# --- NEGATIVE: must not match @import / @import.path ---

# A variable whose value merely contains the words "include"/"subninja" as
# text must not be mistaken for the directives above.
description = include the subninja outputs

# A build edge referencing a file literally named `include.ninja` as an
# input is not itself an include directive.
rule cp
  command = cp $in $out

build out/include.ninja: cp templates/include.ninja
